  "query_preview": "..\nKey Message 1: Shower chances now mainly confined to the western\nmountains. \n\nTonight and early morning Monday should see any lingering rain\nchances confined to the western mountains for more of an \nupslope component. Will see some fog and plenty of stratus for\nthe mountains. Monday daytime looks to be dry under NW flow but\nquite gusty. The gradient winds should weaken by late \nafternoon/evening. \n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...Dry weather into midweek with temps above\nnormal. \n\nBuilding ridge behind Isaias will bring temperatures back to\nabove normal through midweek. Another shortwave and front look\nto arrive anytime between Thursday and Saturday with model\ndifferences abounding. Ensembles/NBM favor some rain chances in\nthe mountains by the end of the week, with limited chances\nacross the Piedmont and temps dropping below normal next\nweekend.",
